### Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal example that shows how to create a card that rotates (3‑D flip) when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card {
    width:260px;
    height:360px;
    perspective:800px;          /* gives depth to the 3‑D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card inner wrapper ---------- */
.card-inner {
    position:relative;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    transition:transform 0.8s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3‑D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* rotate around Y‑axis */
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-face {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;       /* hide backside when turned */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.card-front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* start rotated so it becomes visible on flip */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 6️⃣ Sample content styling ---------- */
.card-front h2,
.card-back h2 {
    margin:0 0 10px;
    font-size:1.4rem;
    color:#333;
}

.card-front p,
.card-back p {
    margin:0;
    font-size:1rem;
    color:#666;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>Hover over me!</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>Here is the other side.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | `perspective` on `.card` | Gives depth to the 3‑D rotation. |
| 2 | `.card-inner` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements in 3‑D space. |
| 3 | `backface-visibility:hidden` on faces | Hides the back side when it’s facing away. |
| 4 | On hover, rotate the inner wrapper 180° around Y axis | Creates the flip effect. |
| 5 | The back face is initially rotated 180° so it becomes visible after the flip. | Aligns the back face with the front when flipped. |

You can replace the sample text, images, or add more styling as needed. Enjoy your rotating card!
